# 146 - Clear Ambush Data on Creature Death

## Status
- Created: 2026-04-04
- Completed: 2026-04-05 (as part of issue 158)
- Phase: 2
- Priority: Low

## Current Behavior
- Creature corpses don't despawn (intentional design)
- When ambush creatures die, `onCreatureDeath` updates player counters
- But dead creatures retain ambush-related data (`ambush-chase-target`, `wander-radius`, etc.)
- Scheduled events may still be registered on the creature object
- This creates memory overhead as corpses accumulate across the world

## Intended Behavior
- When ambush creatures die, all ambush-related data is cleared from them
- Any scheduled events are removed from the creature
- The corpse remains as static scenery (like bones or environmental objects)
- The creature is effectively "detached" from the ambush system on death
- Memory footprint is reduced to just the corpse visual

## Implementation Steps

1. Modify `Ambush.onCreatureDeath` to:
   - Remove scheduled events from the creature via `creature:RemoveEvents()`
   - Clear ambush-related data: `ambush-chase-target`, `wander-radius`, `ambush-max-distance`, `orbit-direction`, `is-rare`

## Technical Notes

### Current Death Handler (line 554-570)
```lua
function Ambush.onCreatureDeath(event, killer, creature)
    local owning_player_ID = creature:GetData("ambush-chase-target") or nil
    local isRare           = creature:GetData("is-rare") or false
    if owning_player_ID then
        local player = GetPlayerByGUID(owning_player_ID)
        if player then
            if isRare then
                player:SetData("is-in-boss-fight", false)
            else
                local numAmbushers = player:GetData("num-ambushers")
                if numAmbushers > 0 then
                    player:SetData("num-ambushers", numAmbushers - 1)
                end
            end
        end
    end
end
```

### Data Fields to Clear
- `ambush-chase-target` - player GUID
- `wander-radius` - orbit radius when player sits
- `ambush-max-distance` - max chase distance
- `orbit-direction` - direction of orbit movement
- `is-rare` - whether this is a rare spawn

